</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>Mechanized tracked platoons move their infantry in armored personnel carriers fitted with tracks for reliable all-terrain performance. Tracked APCs handle mud, snow, rubble, and rough ground better than any wheeled or hover alternative, making these platoons the preferred mechanized infantry for operations where terrain is uncertain or hostile. They sacrifice road speed compared to wheeled formations but gain the ability to keep pace with armored vehicles across broken ground. The APCs provide meaningful ballistic protection during transit, though troops must still dismount to fight effectively.</p><p>Carrying heavy recoilless rifles that fire shaped-charge warheads, these platoons field crew-served weapons heavy enough to threaten armored vehicles at ranges beyond what personal arms can achieve. A rare few are equipped with heavier armor than is commonly found, allowing these teams to assault well protected objectives and hold critical positions as long as possible.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on introduction date of ballistic plate armor.
</notes>

